  "id": "COMPOUND:15061 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Chaxamycin B is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular interactions. The drug acts as a target of multiple compounds, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, all of which are targets of the choline transporter. This suggests that Chaxamycin B may influence the choline transporter through a pathway involving the sialyltransferase enzyme, which is a key player in the synthesis of sialic acid. The presence of multiple targets, including a sialyltransferase and the choline transporter, indicates that Chaxamycin B may act as a modulator of the choline transporter by affecting the enzymatic processes that regulate its activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Chaxamycin B to exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, ultimately influencing the function of the High-affinity choline transporter.",
